{
  "uid": "truss-logs",
  "title": "Truss \u2014 logs",
  "description": "The applier's narration, shipped off the node before its Job is deleted. Error and warning counts are also a Prometheus metric truss pushes itself; the alerts fire on that, so they do not depend on this pipeline.",
  "tags": [
    "truss",
    "logs",
    "loki"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "timezone": "utc",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "loki",
        "label": "Loki",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "loki",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Where these lines come from, and why they are shipped at all",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The applier's pod logs survive about fifteen minutes.** The frequent pass runs every five minutes with `successfulJobsHistoryLimit: 3`, so a successful pass's logs are deleted with its Job three passes later. Every incident in this project's history was investigated from logs; an incident noticed an hour later has none. That is what the collector is for.\n\n**The counts are not from here.** `truss_pass_log_events{level=\u2026}` is a metric truss pushes itself, and the error and warning alerts fire on that \u2014 so alerting does not depend on this pipeline being up. What Loki adds is the part a count cannot give you: *which* warning, on *which* pass, with what message.\n\n`level` is a real label, promoted from truss's logfmt narration by the collector \u2014 so `level=\"error\"` is an index lookup, not a substring scan. Lines that are not logfmt (tofu, git, Vault) keep their content and simply carry no level."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Errors and warnings",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Errors, last hour",
      "description": "An error means something was **lost** \u2014 a ledger object that was not written, a durable record that no longer exists. Not the same as a pass failing: a pass can fail cleanly with no error line at all.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${loki}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({namespace=\"infra\", app=\"applier\", level=\"error\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "instant"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "text": {
          "valueSize": 42
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Warnings, last hour",
      "description": "A warning is something noticed that the pass survived: an alert that could not be sent, a monitor that did not answer, a metrics push that failed. Individually non-fatal; a rising count is the signal.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${loki}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 5,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({namespace=\"infra\", app=\"applier\", level=\"warn\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "instant"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "text": {
          "valueSize": 42
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Errors and warnings over time",
      "description": "Correlate a spike here against the same window on [Truss \u2014 timeline](/d/truss-timeline): a warning burst with no refusal beside it is usually a transport (Telegram, the gateway, the monitor) rather than the applier.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${loki}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 14,
        "x": 10,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({namespace=\"infra\", app=\"applier\", level=\"error\"}[$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "error",
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({namespace=\"infra\", app=\"applier\", level=\"warn\"}[$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "warning",
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "min": null,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "pointSize": 8,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter",
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "normal"
            },
            "axisSoftMin": 0
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "error"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "warning"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "orange"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Every error and warning line",
      "description": "The lines themselves, newest first. The pod each came from travels as structured metadata rather than as a label \u2014 expand a line to see it. It is not a label on purpose: every CronJob run has a new pod name, which would mint a Loki stream per pass.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${loki}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "{namespace=\"infra\", app=\"applier\", level=~\"warn|error\"}",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": false,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Everything the pass said",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Full narration",
      "description": "Every line, including the `tofu` and `git` output that carries no level. This is the panel to read when a refusal's one-sentence reason is not enough \u2014 the plan output that explains it is here and nowhere else fifteen minutes later.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${loki}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "{namespace=\"infra\", app=\"applier\"}",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": false,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Line volume by level",
      "description": "Includes lines with no level \u2014 the unparsed prose from child processes. A pass that suddenly narrates far more than usual is either retrying something or planning a much larger diff.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${loki}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (level) (count_over_time({namespace=\"infra\", app=\"applier\"} | logfmt [$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{level}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": false,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "min": null,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "pointSize": 8,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter",
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "normal"
            },
            "axisSoftMin": 0
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The vault it reads from",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Vault server log",
      "description": "Vault's own startup, seal and error messages \u2014 the other half of any incident involving the credential store.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f This is the SERVER log, not the audit device. The audit log records a request path for every operation and writes to a file or socket rather than stdout; where that evidence lives is a separate decision and nothing here ships it.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "${loki}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "${loki}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "{namespace=\"vault\"}",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": false,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      }
    }
  ]
}